structure; present the *information*.\n\n6.  **Final Output Generation:** (This leads directly to the structured summary provided in the final answer.)","content":"Based on the provided Wikipedia infobox and text, here is a comprehensive summary of the information regarding the wolf (*Canis lupus*).\n\n***\n\n### 🐺 Wolf (*Canis lupus*) Summary\n\nThe content provides detailed taxonomic classification and general information about the **wolf**, scientifically known as ***Canis lupus***.\n\n#### 🧬 Taxonomy\n| Rank | Classification |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Phylum** | Chordata |\n| **Class** | Mammalia |\n| **Infraclass** | Placentalia |\n| **Order** | Carnivora |\n| **Family** | Canidae (Dog family) |\n| **Genus** | *Canis* |\n| **Species** | ***C. lupus*** |\n\n#### 📜 Nomenclature & Origin\n*   **Binomial Name:** *Canis lupus*\n*   **Authority:** Linnaeus, 1758\n\n#### 🗺️ Distribution and Status\n*   The accompanying image displays the **Global wolf range based on IUCN's 2023 assessment.**\n*   Information regarding subspecies is directed to a separate article: \"Subspecies of *Canis lupus*.\"\n\n#### ℹ️ Key Contextual Note\nThe text clarifies that while domestic and feral dogs are included in the phylogenetic definition of the genus, they are not considered part of the colloquial definition of a \"wolf.\"","msg":"LLM response"}
